<!--
  PLACEHOLDER ICON. design-system owns the real icon set (mobile/design-tokens) and it has not
  shipped yet. Concentric arcs, monochrome, because a notification small icon is rendered as a
  silhouette by the system — colour and detail are discarded.

  THE WHITE IS NOT A DESIGN TOKEN AND MUST NOT BECOME ONE. A notification small icon is required
  by the platform to be an opaque-white-on-transparent silhouette; the system then recolours it
  with the device accent. Pointing this at a Radius colour token would be wrong on every device.
  It uses @android:color/white rather than a hex literal so that the "no raw hex under
  mobile/android/" grep stays a real check instead of one with an exception list.

  The 24dp size and the viewport/path numbers are the ASSET'S OWN GEOMETRY, not layout spacing:
  24dp is the platform's notification-icon spec, and path coordinates are not on anyone's 4pt grid.
  They are deliberately not tokenised.
-->
